Defects found:

- **DIFFERENT COPY / hidden text read as visible**: line 113.  
  Input: `html='<html><title>ACS Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel</title><SCRIPT>Review Title Network Meta-Analysis of Direct Oral Anticoagulants Dabigatran Rivaroxaban Apixaban Edoxaban Population Adults with NVAF</SCRIPT><body>No protocol pack here</body></html>'`, `canon={'title':'ACS Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel'}`.  
  Consequence: uppercase `<SCRIPT>` content is not removed, then line 114 strips only the tags, so non-rendered script text produces `FAIL`.

- **idempotency guard satisfied by its OWN comment/marker**: line 158.  
  Input: `html='<html><title>ACS Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel</title><body>Review Title Network Meta-Analysis of Direct Oral Anticoagulants Dabigatran Rivaroxaban Apixaban Edoxaban Population Adults with NVAF</body></html>'`, `canon={'title':'ACS Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel','audit_note':'foreign protocol says Network Meta-Analysis of Direct Oral Anticoagulants Dabigatran Rivaroxaban Apixaban Edoxaban'}`.  
  Consequence: because the vocabulary is all JSON text, an audit/comment field containing the foreign protocol terms makes the contaminated page return `PASS`.

- **merged-cell / off-by-one tabulation error**: lines 147-148.  
  Input: `html='<html><title>Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel Major Bleeding</title><body>Population Intervention Comparator Primary Outcome Nonvalvular atrial fibrillation anticoagulated Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel Major bleeding</body></html>'`, `canon={'title':'Ticagrelor Prasugrel Clopidogrel Major Bleeding'}`.  
  Consequence: adjacent table headers cause the first three fields to be discarded and the value row to be read as `Primary Outcome`, diluting a foreign `Population` into `PASS`.

- **STATUS CODE REPORTING THE WRAPPER rather than the work**: lines 278-281 and 296.  
  Input: run `--corpus` with `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json={"p.html":"bad.json"}`, existing `p.html`, and `bad.json` containing `{`.  
  Consequence: the JSON load failure is silently skipped and the command can exit `0` with that pair unscreened.

No proven defect found for: CRLF/LF text comparison, zero conflated with absent, negation dropped, or probe keyed to a string a fix removes.
